        "evidence": "qu-to-qou-proof.md:32-35: \"total ramification $R_{tot} = 2d + |\\chi(A)|$ by Riemann--Hurwitz: $\\chi(S) = d\\cdot\\chi(\\mathbb{P}(V)) - R_{tot}$\"",
        "notes": "Standard Riemann–Hurwitz is χ(S) = d·χ(base) − R_tot with R_tot ≥ 0 the ramification; here χ(ℙ(V))=2 (so base is ℙ^1). The asserted R_tot = 2d + |χ(A)| would give χ(S) = 2d − (2d+|χ(A)|) = −|χ(A)|, i.e. χ(S) ≤ 0, which is a strong constraint presented as if forced by RH alone — the value 2d+|χ(A)| for R_tot is asserted, not derived (RH gives a relation, not this particular ramification total). Possible quantifier/derivation slip; flagged minor pending the upstream thm statement."
      }
